## Backup and Restore

{% if persistence == 'postgres' and learning_backend != 'postgres' -%}
> **This project has TWO datastores -- back up both.** You generated it
> with `persistence=postgres`, which provisions Postgres for *your
> application code*. The platform's learning store is separate and
> **stays SQLite** (`learning_backend=sqlite`): corrections, feedback,
> trust scores, budget spend, and audit events all live in
> `data/learning.db` on the app host's disk, not in Postgres. A
> deployment pipeline that only dumps Postgres silently loses all
> learned state on every redeploy that recreates the filesystem. Back up
> the SQLite file (next section) on the same schedule as `pg_dump`, and
> mount `data/` on a persistent volume in containerized deployments --
> or set `learning_backend=postgres` (`copier update`) to consolidate.
{%- elif persistence == 'postgres' and learning_backend == 'postgres' -%}
> **Two Postgres databases.** Your app data (`DATABASE_URL`) and the
> learning store (`LEARNING_POSTGRES_DSN`) are separate connections and
> may be separate databases -- `pg_dump` both. Note that with
> `LEARNING_BACKEND=postgres` and no `LEARNING_POSTGRES_DSN`, store
> init raises and learning degrades to no-op (nothing is silently
> written to SQLite instead) -- verify the DSN is set in production.
{%- elif persistence == 'sqlite' and learning_backend == 'sqlite' -%}
> **Two SQLite files.** The app database
> (`data/{{ project_slug }}.db`) and the learning store
> (`data/learning.db`) are separate files; back up both.
{%- endif %}

### SQLite (default)

The learning store is a single file (default `data/learning.db`; the
app database is `data/{{ project_slug }}.db` when `persistence=sqlite`).
Connections run in **WAL mode** (`PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL`), which means
live data can sit in `-wal` / `-shm` sidecar files next to the database.

- **Preferred:** `sqlite3 data/learning.db ".backup 'backup.db'"` --
  safe while the app is running, folds the WAL in.
- **File copy:** only with the app stopped, and copy the `-wal` and
  `-shm` files together with the `.db` if they exist.
- **Restore:** stop the app, replace the file(s), start. Schema
  migrations are forward-only and idempotent -- an older backup is
  upgraded on next startup.

### Postgres (`LEARNING_BACKEND=postgres`)

```bash
pg_dump "$LEARNING_POSTGRES_DSN" --format=custom --file=learning.dump
pg_restore --clean --if-exists --dbname="$LEARNING_POSTGRES_DSN" learning.dump
```

The docker-compose Postgres service (when `persistence=postgres`) stores
data in the `pgdata` volume; back that up on the same schedule.

